+# Preserved protocol and extension
+
+Initial framing is retained verbatim below. TI03 qualifies its event/call premise after reading staff-report p31; historical accounts are not rewritten.
+
+## Initial protocol
+
+# Original archival interview controls for telephone attribution and timing
+
+TEL02/TEL04, AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. FAA cancellation/successor exact searches returned no relevant underlying record and are retained separately, without another public metadata finding. Continue a concrete official-archive source route rather than repeat missing-input summaries.
+
+The held staff report T01 p94/note259 preserves differently attributed Halleck–Herndon contact times from Marquis, Arpey and later AA information. The original NARA interview copies for Marquis and Arpey were not found in the inspected source/acquisition records. The official MFR index supplies exact candidate IDs2609600 and2609591, advertised nine/four pages. These are candidate interview sources, not native carrier logs, proof of unique-call identity or independent clock calibration.
+
+Acquire only the actual catalog-exposed public PDFs if available: two original archival items, maximum thirteen pages total for complete source-context reading. Obtain download links from the actual public catalog, not guessed sequential filenames. The web reader cannot access these catalog pages; use the ordinary public catalog interface, no hidden API, authentication or download gate bypass. No outreach, fee or new request. Preserve URL/catalog relationship, UTC/client date, SHA-256/bytes/pages and exact reading scope. Do not reconstruct redactions or publish raw witness/contact/account data.
+
+Question: what did the interviewees actually say about the contact, who made/heard it, available recordings/logs and time/recollection limits? Compare with the frozen staff-report citation and held Halleck MFR. Identify explicit source/attachment/custody references that can locate the operational original. Preserve source dependence and counterevidence; do not force accounts into one call, choose a preferred time, infer deliberate misstatement or treat a later MFR as a contemporaneous2001carrier event.
+
+If no public body is available, preserve a bounded access/locator TODO and stop that route, with no duplicate public finding. A real new source-level observation may receive an additive reviewed report/checklist/source pins/TODOs/diff and verified AveLyra publication. All original five tracks and eighteen criteria remain unchanged and unfinished; no case outcome, native carrier test or technical-owner recorder/materials work is duplicated or claimed. No mailbox, private case correspondence, deletion, source overwrite, private push, merge or history rewrite.
+
+Separate ready artifact question, not executed by this protocol: the held court ZIP inventory contains uninspected AA 11 Calls.swf, UA 93 Calls.swf, Main.swf and MainNew.swf. Comparing those exact source variants against already studied members could audit presentation version/caller-field provenance, but cannot replace native carrier/operator/recipient joins. Preserve it for a distinct prospective test rather than silently broadening this interview acquisition.
+
+## Prospective extension
+
+# Prospective counterpart check
+
+The actual public catalog for NAID 2609600 describes a November 19, 2003 record and nine paper pages, while its exposed PDF download contains an April 26, 2004 SOC conference-call memorandum in three pages. The first two acquisitions total seven pages, below the original thirteen-page ceiling. Preserve the catalog and downloaded-body associations separately; do not rename the held download to conceal this distinction.
+
+Before any further acquisition, permit inspection of the concrete counterpart NAID 2609603, which the official MFR index describes as an April 26, 2004 SOC interview. Permit at most one additional catalog-exposed PDF of up to nine pages, for at most sixteen PDF pages total. Do not guess a filename. If the counterpart exposes the same URL already held, preserve that new association without repeating the network download. Any differing body is a separate source and requires its own hash and complete page reading. The November 19 nine-page interview remains missing unless its actual body is recovered and inspected. Catalog/body discrepancies remain unresolved, not evidence of replacement, intent, or archive deletion.
+
+All prior privacy, source preservation, ownership, publication and acceptance restrictions remain in force.
+
+## Completed scope
+
+Three acquired PDFs, ten pages, all page images read. Held T01 pp31/94 and T02 pp3/4 reinspected. No native carrier logs, interview audio, ASD/TSD feed, new FAA disposition record or clock test. Search misses remain local rather than being republished as suspicious findings.
